                                <DTC ID="DTCB21CB00" OID="03dce02d-912a-4784-a601-221303245f62">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB21CB00</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10603264</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B21CB00</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1354833736">Hardwire Crash Signal PWM signal</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1788665557">service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1152259587">Check ACU module output</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1719026305">Voltage supply is in the normal range(9V~16v)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1032556202">continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_592668466">20ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_453815806">PWM input frequency and duty cycle is different to the characteristics of normal operation and different to the signal characteristics of crash detection.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_596175441">PWM input frequency and duty cycle is equal to the characteristics of normal operation or equal to the signal characteristics of crash detection.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1126449708">Record DTC</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_740727462">After 100 IGN ON to OFF cycles,clear history DTC automatically</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_2142204756">Signal received by ACU outside ot the normal operation range</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_582394279">Detection of crash via PWM input unavailable</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCB21CC00" OID="8ba80618-8322-4de4-a015-9fd36bcea7dc">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB21CC00</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10603520</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B21CC00</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_2039706830">Battery Saver Short to GND or Over load</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_712048008">no service</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_202844128">Check circuit of Battery Saver lamp</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1719026305">Voltage supply is in the normal range(9V~16v)</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1032556202">continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_592668466">20ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_636748654">The output current  will be checked to monitor the failure, if the current is higher than specific power threshold(based on HW), it's considered as failure.
Battery Saver Short circuit to GND or Over load for 30ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_396783509">Retrigger the output, the output current  will be checked to monitor the failure, if the current is lower than specific power threshold(based on HW), it's considered as No failure.
Battery Saver circuit NOT Short circuit to GND or Over load for 100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_538915992">Record the DTC
Cut off the output
