DRL circuit NOT Short circuit to GND or Over load for 100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_201223724">Record the DTC
Cut off the output
Send CAN Message BCM_RiDRLFlt=0x1</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_740727462">After 100 IGN ON to OFF cycles,clear history DTC automatically</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_820407084">This DTC is detonated if the current is higher than threshold define to this signal, during a determined time.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1242321691">Lower visibility of the vehicle for other drivers.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCB221601" OID="3c5aee87-bccd-4a6b-9975-99d7bac0478c">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB221601</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10622465</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B221601</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1263719025">Right DRL circuit open load/lamp fault</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1788665557">service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1768727158">Check circuit of DRL lamps</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_1621008816">Voltage supply of BCM is in the range of 11-16V
Day-time Running Light  function active for 100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_592668466">20ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_2086439186">The output current  will be checked to monitor the OL failure, if the current is lower than specific HW threshold, it's considered as OL failure or STB failure.Circuit open or short to battery for 100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_268471832">The output current  will be checked to monitor the OL failure, if the current is higher than specific HW threshold, it's considered as No OL failure.
DRL NOT Open load for 100ms
After the output changed to inactive again, the DTC status will be updated.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_415029192">Record the DTC
Send CAN Message BCM_RiDRLFlt=0x1</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_740727462">After 100 IGN ON to OFF cycles,clear history DTC automatically</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_654369116">This DTC is detonated if the current is lower than threshold define to this signal, during a determined time.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1242321691">Lower visibility of the vehicle for other drivers.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCB221715" OID="0c7b910b-1817-4eac-a1ed-04d3ced9b4d9">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB221715</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10622741</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B221715</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1325007398">Left front LED turn light broken, or  feedback line short to battery, or feedback line open load</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1788665557">service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_852315313">Check circuit of turn indicator lamps</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_281654820">Voltage supply of IBC is in the range of 11-16V
Turn Left Light active for 100ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_592668466">20ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_2132192428">100ms after left turn indicator is turned ON and while it remains ON, the Left Front feedback line is read as HIGH for 200ms.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_371907205">Next activation, 100ms after left turned indicator is turn ON and while it remains ON, the Left Front feedback line is read as LOW for 200ms.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_65441694">Record the DTC
Use double frequency blinking for left turn indicators and left side markers for requests other than Hazard lights
Transmit BCM_LeTrunLampOutpCmd with double frequency toggling.
Send CAN Message BCM_LeTurnLampFlt=0x1</SD>
                                            <SD SI="DTC_Aged_Crieria" TI="TI_740727462">After 100 IGN ON to OFF cycles,clear history DTC automatically</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Cause_of_Failure" TI="TI_754228570">The DTC is triggered by feedback lines of the turn indicator lamp embedded logic. It can represent line broken, STB, STG, Open Circuit.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Possible_Impact" TI="TI_1904905887">Driver will not be able to signal other drivers intention to change lanes.</SD>
                                        </SDG>
                                    </SDGS>
                                </DTC>
                                <DTC ID="DTCB221711" OID="f9f4a68a-1b2f-4902-99d7-016b8e7a5ed1">
                                    <SHORT-NAME>DTCB221711</SHORT-NAME>
                                    <TROUBLE-CODE>10622737</TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B221711</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_1735177379">Left front LED turn light feedback line short to ground</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1788665557">service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_852315313">Check circuit of turn indicator lamps</SD>
