                                    <DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>B23C400</DISPLAY-TROUBLE-CODE>
                                    <TEXT TI="TI_971794501">AHL driver motor right communication failure

HeadlampLevelingMotor Communication error RIGHT
signal name : CommMotLostR</TEXT>
                                    <SDGS>
                                        <SDG SI="EXTRAINFO">
                                            <SD SI="Service_Relevant" TI="TI_1788665557">service at next halt</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Repair_Action" TI="TI_1133165657">AML/Johnson recommendations :
1. Check Wiring Harness between LuMEMS and Levellers/motors
2. Check Left motor (actions steps to be defined)
3. Change Left Motor
4. Change LuMEMS ECU</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Enable_Conditions" TI="TI_568240341">ECU is awake and communication active</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Type" TI="TI_1660869490">Continuous</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Monitor_Rate" TI="TI_2022810503">90ms</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Failure_Criteria_Test_Result_NOK" TI="TI_1249046367">LIN signal LIN4:LUM_BCM_4::CommMotLostR has a value of 0x01 for three cycles.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Pass_Criteria_Test_Result_OK" TI="TI_1690199836">LIN signal LIN4:LUM_BCM_4::CommMotLostR has a value of 0x00 for three cycles.</SD>
                                            <SD SI="Limp_home_Action" TI="TI_1746220485">Record the DTC
